#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#Non-linear front suspension compliance properties are used on a vehicle travelling over a small, smooth bump.
#
#The vehicle linked to this example is the Full Size SUV. To see how the non-linear suspension compliance properties were applied to this vehicle:
#
#(1) Browse to the Vehicle: Assembly screen and click on the blue link for the front suspension Springs, Dampers, and Compliance.
#
#(2) On the Suspension: Independent Compliance screen, click on the blue link "SUV, Full Size - Front Compliances."
#
#(3) On the Susp.: Compliance (Nonlinear) screen, note the two Translational Compliance datasets at the bottom of the screen. Both of these datasets are linked to tables showing nonlinear data for the Longitudinal displacement as a function of Fx, and Lateral displacement as a function of Fy.
#
#The small bump was created using data for the incremental elevation and dz ratio seperately. Click on the Procedure blue link "Small Bump", and follow the links for the 3D road to see how this was done.
#
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

LOG_ENTRY Used Dataset: CarSim Run Control; { Suspension and Ride Tests } Non-Linear Suspension Compliance
